<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov vehicle exports up 14.1 pct yr/yr--JAMA.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov vehicle exports up 14.1 pct yr/yr--JAMA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports rose 14.1 percent in November from a year earlier to 329,868 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the sixth successive month of year-on-year gains.  </p>
<p>		     November	YR/YR CHANGE</p>
<p> Cars		257,986	    +17.8</p>
<p> Trucks	     68,469	     +3.4</p>
<p> Buses		 3,413	    -12.4</p>
<p> Total	     329,868	    +14.1</p>
<p>Exports by destination:</p>
<p> Asia		 53,725	     +0.6</p>
<p> Middle East	30,865	    +38.8</p>
<p> Europe	     81,955	     +1.6</p>
<p> - EU		 69,990	     -2.1</p>
<p> North America    111,688	   +34.7</p>
<p> - U.S.	     105,909	   +33.0</p>
<p> Latin America    20,293	    +33.4</p>
<p> Africa	     10,197	    -21.0</p>
<p> Oceania	    20,284	     -4.2</p>
<p> Other		   861	    +36.9</p>
<p>Exports by major manufacturers:</p>
<p> Toyota	 111,256	     +4.5</p>
<p> Nissan	  55,167	    +30.0</p>
<p> Mitsubishi    39,912	    +15.2</p>
<p> Mazda	   37,270	    +25.2</p>
<p> Honda	   34,460	    +17.1</p>
</text>
